  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri G Sandeep Reddy vs State Of Karnataka on 21 October, 2024 -1- Nc: 2024:Khc:42111 Crl.P No. 9977 of 2022 In The High Court Of Karnataka At Bengaluru Dated This The 21St Day Of October, 2024 Before The Hon'Ble Mrs Justice M G Uma Criminal Petition No. 9977 Of 2022 (482(Cr.PC) / 528(Bnss) Between: Sri G Sandeep Reddy Representing M/S Bristo Beverages S/O Chanchireddy Aged 41 Years R/At No 413, Elegant Pride Apremtnet 4Th Cross, Telecom Layout Jakkur Post Bangalore 560 064. ...PETITIONER (BY SRI. EDMOND DANDY, ADVOCATE) AND: 1. STATE OF KARNATAKA BY SAMPIGEHALLI PS REP BY SPP Digitally signed by HIGH COURT OF KARNATAKA LEELAVATHI S AT BENGALURU 560 001. R Location: HIGH 2. M/S MEGA FRUIT PROCESSING PVT LTD COURT OF REP BY SRI VENUGOPAL P C KARNATAKA S/OLT CHENNAPPA GOWDA AGED 32 YEARS OFFICE AT 1-146/B, PATHE HOUSE BELLANDUR, KAIMARA POST KADABA TALUK, DAKSHINA KANNDA DIST. ...RESPONDENTS (BY SMT. RASHMI JADHAV, ADDL.SPP FOR R-1 SRI. VINAYAK KAMATH K., ADVOCATE FOR R-2) -2- Sri G Sandeep Reddy vs State Of Karnataka on 21 October, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/12222052/ 1 NC: 2024:KHC:42111 CRL.P No. 9977 of 2022 THIS CRL.P IS FILED U/S 482 CR.PC PRAYING TO QUASH THE FINAL REPORT C.C.NO28206/2022 DATED 02.08.2022, FOR THE OFFENCE P/U/S 420 OF IPC AND 63 AND 65 OF COPYRIGHT ACT WHICH IS ON THE FILE OF IX ADDL.C.M.M COURT AT BENGALURU. THIS PETITION, COMING ON FOR ADMISSION, THIS DAY, ORDER WAS MADE THEREIN AS UNDER: CORAM: HON'BLE MRS JUSTICE M G UMA ORAL ORDER Petitioner being accused No.1 in Crime No.4/2022 of Sampigehalli Police Station, now pending in C.C.No.28206/2022 on the file of the learned IX Additional Chief Metropolitan Magistrate, Bengaluru, for the offences punishable under Section 420 of the Indian Penal Code (for short \"IPC\") and under Sections 63 and 65 of Copyrights Act, 1957 (for short \"Copyright Act\") is seeking to quash the criminal proceedings initiated against him.",
    "facts": "Even though the petitioner is not a registered copy right holder, he is registered under Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises Development Act, 2006 (for short \"the said Act of 2006\") and accordingly, he is manufacturing and marketing the beverage after getting permission from the Food Safety and Security Authority of India (FSSAI). There is no violation of any of the provisions of the Copyright Act and therefore, the petition is liable to be allowed.",
    "arguments": "He is the owner of M/s. NC: 2024:KHC:42111 Royal Acqua Industries, a start up company manufacturing the beverage by name \"Royal Fizz Jeera Masala\". 4. Learned counsel also submitted that respondent No.2 has filed an application seeking to withdraw the complaint filed by it, inspite of that the Trial Court proceeded with the matter and on that count also, the criminal proceedings is liable to be [LEAKAGE_MASK]. Accordingly, prays for allowing the petition. He is running M/s. Megha Sri G Sandeep Reddy vs State Of Karnataka on 21 October, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/12222052/ 2 Fruits Processing Private Limited and producing beverage under the name and style as \"Bindu Fizz Jeera Masala\"."
  },
